  "note": "A repeat post is an establishment the Ministry of Health registry entered a second time in the language it already had, which the twin-post recovery cannot reach because it only ever pairs a French post with an Arabic one. A few establishments were also entered a second time in the same language; the repeat post is folded into the same record and `refs.msp_repeat` names it, so that id resolves to the record too. This is what the repeat-post merge in packages/sante/scripts/fetch.mjs decided: the pairs it folded into one record, and every candidate it kept apart, with the reason. Candidates come from two signals, two posts of one type and wilaya whose locality folds to the same @geoalgeria/normalize key, and two posts whose whole title folds to the same key; only the second merges, so a name the registry wrote differently stays two records. `conservative_keys` is what the gate reads and `loose_keys` is the second opinion test/sante-repeat-posts.test.mjs holds it to: the loose key has to agree on every pair merged here and to separate every pair kept apart. WordPress's `-N` slug suffix is not used as evidence, because post_name is truncated and the suffix marks a collision on the truncated stem rather than on the title. Every array describes the same two posts, in the same order, as the ids beside it. Regenerated by `npm run fetch` in packages/sante.",
